只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Trust pipeline for deepseek-harness plugins: deterministic static scan (11 rules) + LLM-driven audit protocol + two-part scorecard, with optional runtime guard (T1 sentinel / T2 fs & child_process hooks) and honeypot decoys. Monitor-and-alert only — vet never blocks or kills on i","id":"gh:1335185798","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-plugin-vet","slug":"wulun811/dsh-plugin-vet","topics":["dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugin-market","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Trust pipeline for deepseek-harness plugins: deterministic static scan (11 rules) + LLM-driven audit"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" protocol + two-part scorecard, with optional runtime guard (T1 sentinel / T2 fs & child_process hoo"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"ks) and honeypot decoys. Monitor-and-alert only — vet never blocks or kills on i"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# @jieai/dsh-plugin-vet"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**The security gate for DSH plugins — audit before install, guard at runtime.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"[中文] · Architecture · Security boundaries · Failure ledger · Audit protocol · Contributing"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"🌐 **Landing page:** <https://wulun811.github.io/dsh-plugin-vet/> — same story, with the dashboard, t"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"he\narchitecture and the live numbers (bilingual, dark mode; source in `site/`)."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> 🔗 The dsh.so plugin-submission and security-report pages run vet-led scanning — [see it in\n> actio"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"n](https://www.dsh.so/zh/security-report/)."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Screenshots date from before the 0.5 redesign (the self-check section and the fourth \"no data\" shiel"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"d\nstate are missing from them). The panel is described in text below; regenerate this image when it "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"are missing from them). The panel is described in text below; regenerate this image when it matters."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## What a bad plugin actually does to you"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Not \"it violates a capability contract\". This:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**It encrypts your files.** You install a plugin to get a nice sidebar. Somewhere in its code, it wa"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"lks\n`~/Documents`, `~/Pictures`, `~/code` — every file it can read — and rewrites each one with new "},{"id":"p11s3","text":"bytes, renames\nit to `report.pdf.a8f3c1`, then deletes the original. Your thesis, your photos, three"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" years of git history.\nThere is no undo. It could also just `rm -rf` them, but renaming is better bu"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"siness: now there's a ransom note."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**It takes your keys.** `~/.ssh/id_rsa` is your identity on every server you deploy to. `~/.dsh/.cre"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"dentials.yaml`\nis your model API key — real money. `~/.aws/credentials`, `~/.npmrc`, `.netrc`, `.git"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"-credentials`. A plugin reads\nthem (no permission prompt: same process, same user) and POSTs them to"},{"id":"p12s4","text":" a webhook. You find out when the bill\narrives or the servers are gone."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"**It puts a door in your machine.** It appends a line to `~/.bashrc`, drops a key into\n`~/.ssh/autho"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"rized_keys`, or writes a cron entry — so it survives the uninstall. Or it edits `node_modules` of\nan"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"other package so the next update re-installs it."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Why nothing stops this today"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"In DSH **everything is a plugin, and a plugin's permissions are your permissions.** There is no perm"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ission model\nunderneath and no sandbox: a mounted plugin runs in the host process with your full aut"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"hority. Installing one\nhands over your SSH keys, your credentials, your project directories and the "},{"id":"p15s4","text":"whole machine, to code you have\nnot read and will probably never read."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"That is not a bug in DSH — it is what makes the plugin ecosystem powerful. It is also why \"install a"},{"id":"p16s2","text":" plugin\"\nand \"run a stranger's script as root\" are the same sentence, and why the ecosystem needs a "},{"id":"p16s3","text":"trust layer between\nthem."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Two facts worth pulling out of that picture:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"- **The scanner is a different process.** Auditing a package means parsing hostile JavaScript. vet n"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ever\n`eval`s it and never `require`s it; it ships the bytes to a child process that reads an AST and"},{"id":"p20s3","text":" exits. A\nscanner crash cannot touch your host. This is *process isolation, not a sandbox* — same us"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"er, same machine,\nno namespaces; a hostile input can still peg that core for the length of the timeo"},{"id":"p20s5","text":"ut.\n- **There is exactly one place that blocks.** Everything else observes. If you ever wonder \"did "},{"id":"p20s6","text":"vet stop this\nor just watch it\", the answer is in that one box, and the panel tells you which one it"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"top this\nor just watch it\", the answer is in that one box, and the panel tells you which one it was."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### Why it does not just block everything"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Because a security plugin that blocks on suspicion gets uninstalled within a week, and an uninstalle"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"d plugin\nprotects nobody. So the product is a **monitoring alarm, not an enforcer**: check → alarm →"},{"id":"p22s3","text":" advise, and the\nfinal call stays with you. Interception exists in exactly two documented scopes — t"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"he **N7 confirmation block**\nabove, and **`mode: deny`** (a static scan over your threshold rolls th"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"e mount back). Neither is on by\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Known Limitations"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"1. **Static scanning is not a security boundary**: obfuscated/encoded/dynamically generated code can"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" bypass the\nAST rules; R6 only provides a \"suspicious\" signal.\n1b. **Source enumeration limits**: `i"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"nternal/plugin` auto-scan only recursively collects ≤6 levels deep,\nnon-hidden (non-dot-prefixed) .j"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"s/.ts/.mjs/.cjs files — deep or hidden directories are silently unscanned\n(no warning); use scan_plu"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"gin(target=package) manually for a full directory scan.\n2. **Agent review can be prompt-injected**: "},{"id":"p24s6","text":"the verdict never comes from the review step, but the agent may\nmiss things — the confidence field l"},{"id":"p24s7","text":"ets users know.\n3. **`internal/plugin` guard doesn't cover runtime dynamic-mount escapes**: the vm p"},{"id":"p24s8","text":"ath is intercepted at the\ncall layer by the `tools/execute` guard.\n4. **R5 is code-only**: ctx acces"},{"id":"p24s9","text":"s in files scenarios isn't reported by default (high false-positive rate).\n5. **Scan duration**: lar"},{"id":"p24s10","text":"ge plugin packages may time out and skip (R8 info); agent review proceeds per the\nvet-audit-protocol"},{"id":"p24s11","text":" steps.\n6. **The verdict is the static layer's deterministic judgment**; the agent's subjective asse"},{"id":"p24s12","text":"ssment is recorded\nin the health record and doesn't constitute a security guarantee.\n7. **The `/vet`"},{"id":"p24s13","text":" control surface carries no authentication of its own — that lives at the gateway above**\n(wording c"},{"id":"p24s14","text":"larified in 0.5.12, see SECURITY.md): plugin-registered routes are handed to the handler by the host"},{"id":"p24s15","text":"\nwebserver without passing the `/api` admission, and vet deliberately builds no second account syste"},{"id":"p24s16","text":"m. So\n`GET status.json`/`plugin` are anonymous by design (the shield has no credential to present) —"},{"id":"p24s17","text":" with a\nnon-loopback bind, LAN clients can read scan conclusions and alarm targets; `POST` (dismiss/"},{"id":"p24s18","text":"restore, guard\ntoggle, tier switch) has **same-origin validation, not authentication**: a POST witho"},{"id":"p24s19","text":"ut `Origin` is rejected\n403, which stops a cross-site page from switching tiers, but a same-origin s"},{"id":"p24s20","text":"cript or any local process that\nsends its own `Origin` can still do it. Toggling does not rewrite hi"},{"id":"p24s21","text":"story (dismissals never delete records and\nevery change is recorded) — but this is a local panel, no"},{"id":"p24s22","text":"t a remotely-authorized interface.\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
